usage: paritydesk <command> [flags]

Switch the Claude desktop app between accounts and keep everything else in step.

commands:
  backups      Prune or purge backup generations
  completion   Print a shell completion script
  config       Show, locate or validate the config file
  doctor       Check the installation, folders and app compatibility
  generations  List or show backup generations
  help         Show help for a command
  history      List past runs
  init         Set up paritydesk for the account in the app now
  log          Show the log of a run
  online       Show or drop changes waiting to be applied in Claude
  plan         Preview what a switch would change (approximate)
  profile      Manage profiles
  rebase       Forget every sync base; the next run is a first sync
  recover      Finish or undo an interrupted run
  rollback     Restore a generation without overwriting newer work
  status       Show the active profile and anything pending
  switch       Switch to another profile
  sync         Re-apply the shared state to the active profile
  uninstall    Remove paritydesk's state; every data folder is kept
  verify       Check that the app kept what the last run wrote
  version      Print the version

global flags:
  --app-support-dir string     paritydesk support directory
  --ascii                      ASCII only
  --config string              config file (also PARITYDESK_CONFIG)
  --json                       print one JSON document
  --no-color                   no colour (also NO_COLOR, TERM=dumb)
  --plain                      plain lines, no tables or spinners
  --read-only                  plan only; never write (also PARITYDESK_READONLY=1)
  --state-dir string           state directory (also PARITYDESK_STATE_DIR)
